[% if not private %]
The owner (`[[ github_owner ]]`) may push their own work directly to `main` without a PR or passing CI. CI still runs after a push; releases retain their CI gates. Force-push, deletion, and merge commits remain blocked for everyone.

Other accounts must use a squash PR with passing, up-to-date `ci`. Agents must use PRs and CI even when authenticated as the owner (see `AGENTS.md`). GitHub checks the pushing account, so enforcing a human/agent boundary requires separate credentials.
[% else %]
GitHub Actions is disabled and no ruleset is installed for this private repo on GitHub Free. Run checks locally. Agents still work on branches and open PRs (see `AGENTS.md`).
[% endif %]

## Local patch versions

Install mise, then run `mise run bump:patch:preview` to inspect the next patch tag.
`mise run bump:patch` requires a clean working tree and creates an annotated local
`vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` tag. It does not commit, push, enable Actions, or publish a
release. An existing stable tag on HEAD is reused, so retries do not bump twice.
Follow this project's existing review/release policy before publishing anything.

## Template updates

`.copier-answers.yml` records public inputs and a pinned template source/revision.
Keep it in Git. On a clean update branch, inspect a template change first:

```sh
uvx --from copier==9.19.1 copier update --vcs-ref <reviewed-tag-or-commit> \
  --pretend --overwrite --skip-tasks
```

Then run the same command without `--pretend`, review all changes/conflicts, and
run the project checks before opening a PR. Do not add `--trust`. Preserve local
edits; a successful render alone is not proof that an update or release works.
Template updates retain the existing stack; changing stacks needs fresh planning.
